  "schematicNotes": [
    {
      "id": "note_at_scope",
      "text": "ST185 ANTI-THEFT HARNESS\nHarness side = Deutsch DT sockets (TE), gold 0462-201-1631 (owned stock).\nDevice leads get DT04 pin mates - see NEED-TO-BUY.md, not drawn (device side).\nAll conductors 20 AWG to fit DT size-16 contacts (20-16 AWG).\nTIE-IN = generic butt splice onto the car / fuse-block lead.\nGrounds: 3 generic M6 rings stacked on one cabin stud (max 2 x 20 AWG per ring).\nBundle lengths are estimates - final tape-measure pass sets them.\nFolds into ST185-CabinAccessory in the Option C restructure.",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 2520,
        "y": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "note_at_immob",
      "text": "THE ALARM DOES NOT CUT THE STARTER.\nOur starter is switched by k_str on the Link's Aux 8 / A26. The\nalarm's ground-when-armed output drives a G4X DIGITAL INPUT and the\nECU's own anti-theft function does the fuel and ignition cut.\nLink XtremeX spec: 'Anti-Theft control through digital inputs,\nover CAN or both'. One less relay, and the cut sits inside the ECU\nwhere it cannot be hot-wired around.\nDI accepts a ground-switched input directly - enable the 4k7 pull-up.",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 2520,
        "y": 450
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "note_at_bay",
      "text": "NO RELAY OR FUSE IN THE ENGINE BAY.\nThe siren is in the bay but its feed comes from the cabin block.\nThe park-lamp flash output drives a relay in the CABIN block.",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 2520,
        "y": 900
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n_cavity_notes",
      "text": "CAVITY NOTES - full text of the signals marked * on this drawing\nAlarm module - main harness (D 1: +12V CONSTANT - from cabin fuse block, 5A. Alarm must stay live with the key off.\nAlarm module - main harness (D 2: GROUND - cabin chassis stud, same stud as the rest of the accessory loom\nAlarm module - main harness (D 3: IGNITION SENSE - +12V key-on, tells the alarm the car is running\nAlarm module - main harness (D 4: SIREN + - switched +12V out, 2A. Siren is in the bay, this feed comes from the cabin.\nAlarm module - main harness (D 5: PARKING LIGHT OUT - flashes the park lamps on trigger. Drive the OEM circuit through a relay in the CABIN block, not a bay relay.\nAlarm module - main harness (D 6: DOOR TRIGGER IN - negative. OEM door courtesy switches.\nAlarm module - main harness (D 9: IMMOBILISER OUT - grounds when armed. Goes to a G4X DIGITAL INPUT, not a starter-kill relay. The ECU does the fuel and ignition cut.\nAlarm module - main harness (D 12: SHOCK SENSOR TRIGGER IN - negative, from the sensor's signal pin\nshock (label): Shock / tilt sensor (replaces the OEM glass-break sensor)\nStatus LED (dash) 2: LED cathode to ground. Kit LED - module limits the current.\nt_at_12v: +12V CONSTANT, 5A from the cabin fuse block. NOT the engine bay.\nt_at_gnd: Cabin chassis ground stud M6 - ring A (alarm + siren)\nt_at_door: OEM door courtesy switches - negative when a door opens\nt_at_hood: Hood pin switch - ADD ONE, the car has no factory hood pin\nt_at_park: Park lamp flash - to a relay in the CABIN block, never a bay relay\nt_at_gnd_b: Cabin chassis ground stud M6 - ring B (shock + LED)\nt_at_12v_shk: +12V CONSTANT, 2A fuse, cabin fuse block - shock sensor feed",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 2520,
        "y": 1080
      }
    }
  ],
